======================================================================
 Dario Store: review from the chat + "Close chat" button
 Date:     2026-09-26 01:50:52 CET
 Branch:   main @ a13ecdb (changes not committed yet)
======================================================================

SUMMARY
  Feature 1  Once an order is DELIVERED, the customer gets a review card at the end of the chat:
             stars, optional message, "hide my name"; saved through the normal review action
             (buyers only, name masking and product rating updates all still apply).
  Feature 2  The chat no longer depends on the order status to stay open (only a cancelled
             order's chat closes by itself). The team (admin and staff) has a "Close chat" /
             "Reopen chat" button; the customer is told in the chat, in their language.
  Database   one new nullable column Order.chatClosedAt (additive, no data changed).
  IMPORTANT  "npm run db:update" was writing to a LOCAL Postgres, not to the Supabase database
             the app uses (see "Database" below). Fixed in prisma.config.ts.
  Tests      226 passed in 19 files (21 new); typecheck, lint and production build pass.
  Live       checked in a real browser (Playwright, production build) as customer and staff,
             with temporary zz- test data that was deleted afterwards.

======================================================================
HOW IT WORKS
======================================================================
Customer side (order page chat):
  - DELIVERED order: a "Delivered / How was your order?" card after the messages, one entry per
    product still in the shop. Already reviewed: stars + "Reviewed" + "Edit" (opens the form
    filled in). Reviews can still be posted when the chat is closed.
  - Chat closed by the store: the message box is replaced by "The store closed this
    conversation. Need anything else? Contact us and we'll reopen it."
Team side (admin order page, admin and staff):
  - "Close chat" button next to the chat title (asks for confirmation). Posts "The store closed
    this conversation. Thanks for your order!" in the chat (customer's language), then nobody
    can write. "Reopen chat" posts "The store reopened this conversation."
  - Not shown on cancelled orders (their chat stays closed; the server refuses to reopen).
  - Team members never see the review card.

Rules on the server (not just hidden buttons):
  - MessageService.send refuses messages in a closed chat, from either side
    (errors.chatClosedByStore), and in a cancelled order's chat (errors.chatClosed).
  - MessageService.setClosed: team only (accessFor with the team side), customers and guests
    get errors.writeDenied; setChatClosedAction requires ADMIN or STAFF.
  - ReviewService.forOrderChat: only the order's owner, only once DELIVERED.

Files:
  src/prisma/contract.prisma (+ contract.json/.d.ts)  Order.chatClosedAt
  src/prisma/orders.ts                                OrderRepository.setChatClosed
  src/services/messages.ts                            closure, setClosed, review in open()
  src/services/reviews.ts                             ReviewService.forOrderChat
  src/actions/messages.ts                             setChatClosedAction (team)
  src/components/chat/ChatReviewCard.tsx (new)        the review card
  src/components/chat/OrderChat.tsx, useOrderChat.ts  button, closed notes, card
  src/styles/chat.css                                 .chatHead, .chatReview* (tokens only)
  src/i18n/messages/en.ts + fr.ts                     new texts in both languages
  prisma.config.ts                                    loads .env (see below)
  CLAUDE.md                                           db:update note, chat-closing rule

======================================================================
DATABASE: what happened and what was fixed
======================================================================
1. Local:    npm run db:update (dry run first): 1 additive operation
             ALTER TABLE "public"."order" ADD COLUMN "chatClosedAt" timestamptz -> applied.
2. Problem:  creating the test order failed with "column order.chatClosedAt does not exist".
             Cause: npm run db:update does not read .env, so prisma.config.ts used its fallback
             postgresql://...@localhost:5432/membership (a local Postgres), while the app uses
             DATABASE_URL from .env (Supabase, aws-0-eu-central-1.pooler.supabase.com:6543).
             The column had been added to the local database only.
3. Supabase: dry run with .env loaded: exactly 1 additive operation, nothing dropped
             (warning shown: "control policy suppressed: namespace __unbound__", informational).
             Applied: "Applied 1 operation(s) across 1 space(s), signature updated".
             Second dry run: "Planned 0 operation(s)".
4. Fix:      prisma.config.ts now does import "dotenv/config" (like src/lib/auth.ts), so
             npm run db:update targets the app's database. A DATABASE_URL exported in the shell
             still wins (dotenv never overrides it). Checked: npm run db:update -- --dry-run now
             plans 0 operations against Supabase.
   Note:     the local Postgres (localhost:5432/membership) also got the column; harmless.
             Earlier schema changes were already in Supabase (its plan showed only this one
             column), so nothing else was missing there.

